-- run: `foldl` and `foldr` left `foreign` in the same commit as the loop
-- (`docs/design/backend.md` §8, "`foldl` and `foldr` leave `foreign`"). They
-- were the only `foreign` values in the repository with a function type
-- anywhere in them, and a JavaScript loop cannot park when its beni callback
-- suspends; core is compiled into the binary, so a beni `foldl` without the
-- loop is a stack bomb in core itself.
--
-- `foldr` is reverse-then-`foldl`, exact for this argument order, and
-- `reverse` is `foldl xs [] cons`, so there is no cycle. `List.range` builds
-- its list with `rangeHelp`, which was already a beni self tail call and
-- simply stops overflowing — the three of them survive twenty thousand cells
-- here, where a non-tail recursion over a list overflows Node's default stack
-- at about 8 000, which is what `bench/runtime/c1`'s blocks-of-500 scaffolding
-- worked around.
import List
import Node exposing (Program)
import String


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines
        [ String.fromInt (List.foldl (List.range 1 20000) 0 (λx acc -> x + acc))
        , String.fromInt (List.foldr (List.range 1 20000) 0 (λx acc -> x + acc))
        , String.fromInt (List.length (List.map (List.range 1 20000) (λn -> n * 2)))
        , String.fromInt (List.foldr [ 1, 2, 3 ] 0 (λx acc -> x - acc))
        ]
